  "output": "The book follows a brass-rank magitech artificer who takes a routine guild job in a ruin that is folded out of space and stuck in a single looping hour [1]. The story involves a party of characters—including a mage, a front-liner, and a scout—who discover that the location, known as the Nine, is \"wrong\" [2, 3]. The narrative explores themes regarding the \"Facets\" of magic, which are shattered tiers of magic where the deep ones are considered lost or forbidden [4].\n\nThe protagonist is **Cael Ferren**, a 26-year-old brass-rank artificer [2, 5]. She has spent her life hiding the fact that she can secretly feel the \"deep Facets\" of magic, a sensation she previously believed to be a sickness [1, 5]. While she initially desires an unremarkable career at the Commission Hall, she eventually learns that the \"hum\" she feels is actually a \"compass to a magic the world broke on purpose\" [5].",
